+ *     which powers the touch controller (AVDD 3.0V on LDO3, DVDD 1.8V on
+ *     LDO2).  There is no RPMh rail for it on this board.
+ *   - Samsung S6SY761 touch controller at 7-bit address 0x48 on GENI I2C
+ *     i2c@a8c000 (QUP wrapper 1, SE index 3), interrupt on TLMM gpio 120.
+ *   - MAX77705 fuel gauge at 0x36 and charger at 0x69 on GENI I2C
+ *     i2c@a88000 (QUP wrapper 1, SE index 2).
+ *
+ * The GENI programming below is the same sequence the SWEET driver uses for
+ * its SE7 touch port (bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c, patch 0060 plus the FIFO
+ * packing fix of 0063), restricted to what these three chips need: no DMA,
+ * no GSI, polled FIFO transfers, 100 kHz.  It is kept private to this file
+ * so the SM7150 code path is untouched.
+ *
+ * Everything here is polled from kernel threads; no hardware interrupt is
+ * used.  The touch controller is not reset by a GPIO on this board (there is
+ * none wired to the SoC): the bootloader leaves the rails on
+ * (regulator_boot_on in both the vendor and the mainline DT), so the IC is
+ * already in application mode when this runs.
+ */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_STARQLTECHN)
